{
  "Description": "First regression case for solid.hollow, on simple bodies only: a box, a trapezoid prism (both x sides slanted, all edges convex), a cylinder cut by a plane tilted by 30 degrees, a half torus and a ball cut by two parallel planes. Every body is hollowed with the wall thickness 2 and its top or cut faces open; the box is additionally hollowed without open faces into a closed body with an enclosed cavity. More complex solids follow in a separate case.",
  "Expected": "All values in closed form. The wall is the solid minus its inward offset by 2, where the inner walls are extended through the open faces: the rim lies in the surface of the open face, not perpendicular to the wall. BOX 40x30x20 (V 24000), top open: 24000-36*26*18 = 7152, 11 faces (5 outer, 5 inner, 1 planar rim with a hole), area 4000+3168+264 = 7432. Closed: 24000-36*26*16 = 9024, a body with an enclosed cavity. PRISM: trapezoid 40 (bottom) / 20 (top) by 20 high, 30 long, V = 18000. The cavity has the width 40-z-2*sqrt(5) for z in 2..20 (the inner slanted walls continue up to the top plane) and the length 26, so the wall is 18000-(29-2*sqrt(5))*18*26 = 6520.9596, of the same thickness 2 up to the rim. CYLINDER r=15 up to the plane z = 30 + x*tan(30deg), V = 225*30*pi = 21205.7504. The cavity is r<13 from z=2 up to the oblique plane - a tube sawn at 30 degrees; the mean height of the plane over any disk around the axis is 30, so the wall is 225*30*pi - 169*28*pi = 2018*pi = 6339.7340. The rim in the oblique plane is 2 wide at the sides and 2/sin(60deg) = 2.309 wide at the highest and lowest point. HALF TORUS R=30 r=8, V = 64*30*pi^2 = 18949.6405; the rims are planar annuli in y=0: pi^2*30*(64-36) = 840*pi^2 = 8290.4677. SPHERE BAND r=20 between z=-10 and z=10, V = pi*(20*400-2000/3) = 23038.3461; the cavity is the ball of radius 18 between the same planes, so the wall is pi*20*(400-324) = 1520*pi = 4775.2208, with planar rims in z=10 and z=-10 from radius sqrt(224) = 14.967 to sqrt(300) = 17.321.",
  "CaseStatus": "KnownFail",
  "Status": "NOT YET IMPLEMENTED (2026-09-26). solid.hollow was changed to a single inward 'thickness' and is a stub that throws NotImplementedException, so every solid.hollow call fails for now. When it is implemented: run the case with Regenerate, compare the results with 'Expected', add the 'verified' notes and set CaseStatus to Ok.",
